    "body": "Took a brief look at this this afternoon and I'm not sure I follow the above logic. Specifically, `specifier` here is supposed to already be a normalized URL, since it should already have gone through sorting and normalizing a module specifier map for the scope per the original parsing.\n\nSo there should be no `\"../resources/\"` key in the scope at merge time, instead it should be `\"https://base/resources/\"`.\n\nThen when doing the merge, the fix should surely be to do the check against the URL-resolved specifiers. i.e. checking `record`'s specifier as a URL first, and treating these as two separate specifier cases - both URL-like versus both bare specifier-like.\n\nPlease let me know if I'm missing anything and thanks for the quick investigation here.",
