    "body": "> Assuming in the above you're talking about normalized URLs though, the semantics around switching the ordering of the check makes complete sense to me.\n\nYes, the _specifier_ from the _newImportMapImports_ and the _record's specifier_ from the _resolved module set_ are both normalizedSpecifiers.\n\nSee Step. 6.1.1 from\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#merge-existing-and-new-import-maps\n\n\nFor reference,\nWhen a module is [added to the resolved module set](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-resolution-algorithm:add-module-to-resolved-module-set),\nthe _specifier_ is normalized.\n\nSame for the _specifierKey_ in the import map's imports\nIt is normalized during [sort and normalize a module specifier map](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#sorting-and-normalizing-a-module-specifier-map), Step 2.1\n\n> 2.1 Let normalizedSpecifierKey be the result of [normalizing a specifier key](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#normalizing-a-specifier-key) given specifierKey and baseURL.\n\n",
